 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**No, not by recent standards. The Aussie is buying more yen than it was a year or two ago.**\n\n- **Latest (16 Oct 2026):** A$1 = ¥109.67\n- **Past month:** about ¥110, stable since mid-September, down from ¥114.63 on 1 Sep 2026.\n- **2026 high:** about ¥114–114.5 in April and August 2026 (monthly closes).\n- **One year ago:** about ¥91–94 (April–June 2025 lows were around ¥91.4).\n- **Start of 2024:** ¥97.05 (January 2024).\n\nSo the Aussie has strengthened against the yen over the past 18 months, rising roughly 20% from its April 2025 low. It has eased from its 2026 peak but is still well above levels from 2024 and 2025. The yen is weak in this comparison, which is why the Aussie buys more of it.",
